WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.460
- The second rule for
arguing, know your stuff.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.830
As I said, this makes you a better person

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:04.920
and it also makes you a better debater

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.540
if you actually know the
material that you're arguing.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.640
I'm not just talking talking points.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.130
I'm talking about know your own worldview.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.270
I'm talking about you
should have a worldview

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.630
that can explain why certain
rights are self-evident.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.930
You should understand why the founders

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.180
thought what the founders thought.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.220
You shouldn't just read the
founders and take it as gospel.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.277
Instead what you should
do is you should say,

00:00:19.277 --> 00:00:21.597
"Okay, what was the root
of the founders' thought?

00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:23.240
"Was that a good argument
or a bad argument?"

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.810
Because the truth is
that when Jefferson says

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.120
in the Declaration of Independence,

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.265
that these truths are self-evident,

00:00:27.265 --> 00:00:28.900
by its own terms that is not true.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.890
Obviously, these truths
are not self-evident.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.040
Right, there are literally
billions of people

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.890
all over the world who
don't believe these truths

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.560
that all men are created equal and endowed

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.940
by their creator with
certain unalienable rights.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.690
Alright, literally billions
of people do not believe this

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.870
and the vast majority of people throughout

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.100
human history have not believed this.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.420
What Jefferson actually meant
when he said self-evident,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.877
he said, "Self-evident to anyone

00:00:46.877 --> 00:00:48.317
"who has thought this stuff through

00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:51.130
"in light of right, reason,
and Judeo-Christian values."

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.450
which means that it's
up to you to actually

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.930
do your reading and know your stuff.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.410
So, you know, this is why I am gonna

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.510
put up a reading list on my website.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.430
This is why YAF has its own reading list.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.840
Do your reading, eat your vegetables,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.270
and then you can know things,
and knowing things is fun

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.524
because the left doesn't know anything.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:07.357
(audience laughs)

